A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=8\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=10\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =40\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{20\\sqrt{2}}{40} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329720 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00626454-06b5-5255-8b10-a969634f2a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326940} {:answer/id #uuid "0a118cb1-bcf0-5192-ac99-50c6d218a0df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327022} {:answer/id #uuid "880cd774-4b0c-578b-9cb7-2a7f6ddc9ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328104} {:answer/id #uuid "9c24e516-7c4c-59ff-9120-8f3e8f967303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328284} {:answer/id #uuid "e1eb75a8-96e9-5751-9380-e070f3e6a153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "880cd774-4b0c-578b-9cb7-2a7f6ddc9ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328104} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cbb3be6-5963-5d28-9797-4fa8242fb4a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329419}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ffe80f4-577a-5763-8b79-42fa1192abfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-43328" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2a9f5e6149b62b5724de8a46e50e7aac2976ffa2f9f841c64417ffd248fcb88.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find the measure of $∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}} & =\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329721 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55cfe684-dc18-5ab1-b164-6d50fade618a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327676} {:answer/id #uuid "8d23ee9d-454e-5907-a98d-d759e11996ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328151} {:answer/id #uuid "b7359851-720e-5ab4-876a-6265d25f515d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328528} {:answer/id #uuid "cf531d87-8a79-5162-b024-e25dc07d7e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328757} {:answer/id #uuid "e7164a97-e526-5ef2-8ced-7e38b414e248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf531d87-8a79-5162-b024-e25dc07d7e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328757} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc9b871-5875-5e5c-8a91-d0aec6bf5882" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329619}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55d7cd50-6834-55b6-a52f-4f6d251b49dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-43339" :question/problem "![](images/85/85b13f2236c5f00da34ea71fdbfc967882fa6e66c347f6ef40c0604391a5d68e.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049d033e-9ea7-58bc-bb55-6b11185d1b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "049d033e-9ea7-58bc-bb55-6b11185d1b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556352} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eaa9ff4-4551-5f33-ba72-289eaa72b4fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556373}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0921e1f0-6016-5a9a-b00a-281e162349d5" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa571435e7a44532cfb3bc61965b56b10e83c090236349851971e1b51c007ade.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{11}{2}\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ Use $\\sin30^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Then, $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=2\\text{ cm} \\\\ b & =AC \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{11}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{11}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 2\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{11}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{\\frac{11}{2}}{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\ b & =11\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=11\\,\\text{cm}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff2e4436-f636-5aa3-88e5-00bf7a733fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff2e4436-f636-5aa3-88e5-00bf7a733fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556405} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce102e6e-9d86-54c9-b424-61ab30bebf30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556394}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1f90245f-9fc6-5863-a434-c42642a9ebf6" :question/problem "![](images/76/76bdcef8f267043fe1f9c97f989ff3d6bfdf3b071158501cf43aef78976e93eb.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64}\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ Then, $AC=${{field-1}} $\\