t {:answer/id #uuid "ba510cf0-a3a0-5d06-8f32-bab53002d3b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556389} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ba1fed-347d-5277-b120-1a48f185cceb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556386}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9cd422c2-0775-5873-a783-f544ad93d54d" :question/problem "![](images/3f/3f14b28ecb2ab34328e461e66b6c00c5516b99d559e675db06306f804d5aaf29.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is $21\\,\\text{mm}^{2}.$ Use $\\sin30^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=7\\text{ mm} \\\\ b & =AC \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 21 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\ 21 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 7\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ 21 & =\\frac{7}{4}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{21}{\\frac{7}{4}} \\\\ b & =12\\text{ mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=12\\,\\text{mm}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556384 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e9829a6-c87f-5189-a880-168c6d74d94d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556356} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6abb05-37ef-5299-9ef6-0a9a17779c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556372} {:answer/id #uuid "9837de89-45e1-5819-b1cc-f2b9b2eb134c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{700}{3}\\,\